From 2d7987449b7ad2ada0b0c67c36ba4271ace75cc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valisolaris <valisolaris@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 18:35:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] windows-port: wrap the pane tab bar into two rows when tabs
 overflow

Adds tabs.max_rows (default 2) so a pane's tab bar grows to a second
row instead of only horizontal-scrolling when its tabs don't fit.
pane_parts_for_rect now takes each tab's rendered label width and
decides bar height (1 or 2) from the same reservation draw_tab_bar
uses, so layout and rendering never disagree on where a row wraps.
draw_box's side borders and tab_drop_target_at's drag-and-drop target
resolution are generalized to respect however many rows the bar has;
push_resize_hits is intentionally left untouched (row 2 stays a dead
zone, matching the existing top-row-only resize handle). Falls back to
the existing single-row + arrow-scroll behavior when max_rows=1, the
pane is too short (height < 5), or everything still fits in one row.
